[1442.069273,"o","\u001b[0m\u001b[H\u001b[2J\r\n  Define the shared virtual gateway\r\n  =================================\r\n\r\n  Priority 200 makes Ze preferred over keepalived's 100. VRID 12 gives\r\n  both routers virtual MAC 00:00:5e:00:01:0c for VIP 203.0.113.1.\r\n\r\n  The rfc5798-compatible checksum interoperates with keepalived's VRRPv3.\r\n  accept-mode true lets the non-owner answer our explicit VIP ping.\r\n  This merges the group into the existing zeptrk0 IPv4 unit.\r\n"]
